{
  "name": "Klein quartic Coxeter complex (omnitruncated / flag graph)",
  "description": "The flag graph (chamber system) of the Klein quartic's (2,3,7) triangle-group tessellation: vertices are the 336 flags (chambers), in bijection with the elements of PGL(2,7) (the full automorphism group of the Klein quartic, order 336). Each vertex has degree 3, one edge per Coxeter generator r1, r2, r3, giving the 'fully truncated' tiling with 84 square faces (from the dihedral relation (r1 r3)^2=1), 56 hexagonal faces (from (r2 r3)^3=1), and 24 14-gonal faces (from (r1 r2)^7=1). Constructed as the Cayley graph of PGL(2,7) with respect to three involutions r1, r2, r3 satisfying the Coxeter relations of type (2,3,7): r1^2=r2^2=r3^2=(r1 r2)^7=(r2 r3)^3=(r1 r3)^2=1, verified computationally to generate the full 336-element group acting on the projective line over GF(7).",
